        // cursor that never had a full block beneath it. The guard sits HERE
        // rather than before the vector loop because the tail has TWO entry
        // paths, and the vector one hands over `base - 1` — which is -1 when
        // the last block started at 0, so a guard only at the top leaves that
        // path reading [data - 1].
