        // arm64_native owed nothing for this, which is not what §3.4's note
        // on self-host assemblers would have predicted: that note was written
        // when this file's whole SIMD surface was cnt/addv, and the string
        // kernels had to add ld1/cmeq/cmlt/shrn/dup by hand. It has since been
        // regenerated from cmd/arm64tblgen, so fmul arrives as part of the
        // three-register lane-wise FP class across 2s/4s/2d, ld1/st1 take
        // every lane arrangement, and dup's mask admits all four sizes. The
        // self-host assembler still needs checking separately; it just now
        // answers the same way its native twin does.
